Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> Rodan wrote:
>
>> I meant more artifacts generated makes it harder to wish for
>> artifacts.
>
> Correct. If you get an early wish, and if you want to spend it
> on an artifact weapon, you'll have better chances if there are
> not yet too many already existing.

Timing is an important factor -

Artifacts are important for survival in the early game.  Wishes become
guaranteed at the start of the late game and are rare in the early game.
If you get a wish in the early game high quality armor has more value
than a high quality weapon.

And so is game skill -

If you have the skill to go without artifacts at all until the Castle,
have fun wishing for the exact artifact you want but completing your
ascension kit should take priority.

If you altar dance for artifacts in the early game, you still need to
have a complete ascension kit before spending wishes on more artifacts.

If you plan on ascending without a complete ascension kit it hardly
matters if your Castle wishes are wasted or not, but the chances are
against someone wanting one specific artifact at the Castle thinking the
others are not worth carrying being able to pull off an ascension
without a complete kit.

> There are many necessary things to have - and if you don't have
> got them to wish for them - than to wish for an artifact weapon;
> since you can get artifacts from sacrificing why wish for one,
> spend the wishes on the essentials and get the artifact weapons
> "for free".

Exactly.  Sometimes the question asked says a lot about the person
asking the question.  In this case it suggests too much value on a
specific artifact for lack of knowing how to use the other artifacts. 
It suggests too much value on weaponry for lack of knowledge of armor. 
It suggests a focus on specific features for lack of knowing how to use
a rich assortment of items.

Is Magicbane being wished for to inscribe the E-word?  I have used a
Castle wish for "blessed +3 rustproof athame".  The only part of that
that ever fails is the "blessed +3" part or the "Nothing happens"
message.


